@* Shared dialog chrome for EVERY dialog in the repo — the sibling of
   DialogShellFooter (and of ReadOnlyDialogShell for the read-only case).

   It renders FluentUI v5's <FluentDialogBody> around ChildContent. That is the
   whole point: in v5 the dialog header is NOT rendered by the FluentDialog host
   and NOT by FluentDialogInstance — it renders only inside FluentDialogBody,
   which owns the title slot (FluentSlot.DialogTitle), the close (X) slot
   (FluentSlot.DialogTitleAction for a dialog, FluentSlot.DialogClose for a
   drawer) and the footer-action slot. A v5 dialog that omits
   <FluentDialogBody> compiles and runs, renders its body, and silently ships
   TITLE-LESS and X-LESS: v4's FluentDialogHeader/FluentDialogFooter were
   removed (MigrationFluentDialog.md §"FluentDialogHeader and FluentDialogFooter
   removed") and nothing in the build flags the omission.

   The title comes from DialogOptions.Header.Title (BuildShellOptions sets it);
   the close (X) routes to the dialog's cancel path with no per-dialog plumbing:
   FluentDialogInstance.OnInitializedAsync wires Header.CloseAction.OnClickAsync
   to DialogShellBase.OnActionClickedAsync(primary: false) → HandleCancelAsync().
   CloseAction.Visible = true is required for the X to display at all
   (DialogOptionsHeaderAction.ToDisplay is false while Visible is false, and
   Visible defaults to false) — BuildShellOptions sets it for every dialog it
   builds options for, so both the shell dialogs and the read-only dialogs get
   the X.

   Usage — it wraps the dialog's WHOLE body, i.e. it is the outermost element of
   the dialog's markup, with the existing root (the EditForm, the root div, or
   ReadOnlyDialogShell) inside it:

     <DialogShellBody>
         <EditForm Model="Model" OnValidSubmit="HandleSubmitAsync">
             ... form fields ...
             <DialogShellFooter Saving="@Saving" Error="@Error"
                                OnCancel="HandleCancelAsync" />
         </EditForm>
     </DialogShellBody>

   The footer is NOT part of this component: DialogShellFooter stays where it is
   today, inside the EditForm it submits. Parameters:
     ChildContent — the dialog's body: the form (shell dialogs) or the
                    list/grid root (read-only dialogs). *@

<FluentDialogBody>
    @ChildContent
</FluentDialogBody>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The dialog's body — everything except the footer. For a
    /// <see cref="DialogShellBase{TModel, TResult}"/> dialog that is the markup
    /// holding the <c>&lt;EditForm&gt;</c> (which itself holds the
    /// <see cref="DialogShellFooter"/>); for a read-only dialog it is the
    /// content root (<see cref="ReadOnlyDialogShell"/> or the dialog's own root
    /// element).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
